  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p5); its Total column prints transfers only as the net (12,000), so transfers_in/out are the fund-column figures (Street +14,057, Sales Tax -26,057). Business-type lines from the modified cash basis proprietary funds statement Total column (p7), incl. nonoperating grant, loan principal and interest; beginning 250,737 and ending 339,634 tie to the government-wide figures. Sewer grant revenue 27,610 is printed as 'Federal grants' on the proprietary cash flow statement (pp8-9). Proprietary cash flows not recorded (cash basis, as in later years). Cash: governmental funds balance sheet cash and cash equivalents 194,887 (ending_cash), certificates of deposit 58,848 (ending_investments), county treasurer cash 3,717 printed separately; beginning cash not printed (null). Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p13, more detailed; the General Fund budget schedule p10 is not recorded to avoid double counting; it prints Police protection 16,600 = Interlocal agreements, and General government 155,962 which includes the General department capital outlay 49,142); Street and Sales Tax Fund budget schedules (pp11-12); proprietary statement-column detail not recorded (as in later years); the Keno Fund has no schedule and is not in detail. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
